<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles VIII of France</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1470–1498</span> · Also known as Charles the Affable</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles VIII was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from 1483, governed in his minority by his sister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-france">Anne of France</a> and her husband Peter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a>. In 1491 he married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-brittany">Anne of Brittany</a>, bringing the duchy under French control. His invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1494 to claim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a>. He died childless after striking his head on a door lintel at Amboise.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-viii-of-france.jpg" alt="Charles VIII of France" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous / After Jean Perréal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_King_Charles_VIII_of_France_(1470%E2%80%931498),_by_anonymous_artist,_16th_century_(cropped)_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
